# Placeholders only. No secret belongs in this file. Nothing loads it
# automatically: the Go server reads the real process environment, so export
# the variables or prefix the command with `env`. See docs/development/getting-started.md.

# Go server (services/core). Defaults are shown. Every value is validated at
# start-up and a wrong or unknown MORNINGSTAR_* variable stops the server.
#
# The listen address must be a loopback IP literal. Wildcard, LAN and
# hostname values are refused.
# MORNINGSTAR_HTTP_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8080
#
# Exact Host header allow-list, comma separated. Loopback names only.
# Default: the listen address and localhost on the same port.
# MORNINGSTAR_HTTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=127.0.0.1:8080,localhost:8080
#
# Exact Origin allow-list of the web UI, comma separated. Loopback http origins
# only. A state-changing request must send an Origin from this list.
# Default: http://127.0.0.1:3000,http://localhost:3000
# MORNINGSTAR_HTTP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://127.0.0.1:3000,http://localhost:3000
#
# debug, info, warn or error
# MORNINGSTAR_LOG_LEVEL=info
# json or text
# MORNINGSTAR_LOG_FORMAT=json

# Database. The cluster is a per-user PostgreSQL 18 that listens on a unix
# socket only and accepts peer authentication only (D-67). There is no host,
# port, user, password or connection string setting, so none can be supplied.
# The directory of the socket. An absolute, clean path of at most 90 bytes.
# Default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/morningstar/pg-run, or ~/.local/share/morningstar/pg-run.
# MORNINGSTAR_DB_SOCKET_DIR=
#
# Owner-only directory for the recovery marker (recovery-generation.md). It must
# stay outside the backup set. Default: $XDG_STATE_HOME/morningstar, or
# ~/.local/state/morningstar.
# MORNINGSTAR_STATE_DIR=

# Directory of the evidence files (D-62, D-77). An absolute, clean path. It is
# created with mode 0700 and refused when it is a symlink, belongs to another
# user or is open to the group or others. Evidence is user data, so the default
# is under the data directory. Default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/morningstar/evidence, or
# ~/.local/share/morningstar/evidence.
# MORNINGSTAR_EVIDENCE_DIR=

# Largest artifact in bytes, from 1 to 67108864. Default 8388608 (8 MiB, approved
# as the provisional MVP limit). An artifact is held in memory while it is
# redacted and while it is served.
# MORNINGSTAR_EVIDENCE_MAX_BYTES=8388608

# The bootstrap secret of the first account is written under XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
# (for example /run/user/1000) and only when that directory is on tmpfs or
# ramfs. It is read from the environment and has no override. When it is unset
# or on disk, account setup is refused.

# Web UI (apps/web). Origin of the Go API for the same-origin rewrite.
# Read by next.config.ts when `next build` or `next dev` starts. Changing it
# needs a new build. Loopback hosts only. May be set in apps/web/.env.local,
# which Git ignores. The Go server accepts this name and ignores its value, so
# it can sit in the same shared environment.
# MORNINGSTAR_API_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:8080
